  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who engage with internet humor that relies on ableist stereotypes and derogatory language, particularly those who find amusement in mocking people with developmental disabilities. The meme is designed to appeal to an audience that understands and uses internet slang like 'lmfa' and appreciates cruel, offensive jokes that target disability, using the false claim of 'Harvard acceptance' to mock intellectual capacity. This audience is likely familiar with ableist tropes and may be drawn to the meme's shock value and dark humor, even though it is hateful and offensive.",
